entry.sense:
to sing, Il., etc.:then of any sound,
to twang, of the bowstring, Od.;
to whistle, of the wind, Mosch.;
to ring, of a stone struck, Theocr.

that may be taken or
conquered, Hdt.;
that may be understood, Plat.

of or
for fishing, Xen., Arist.; h( a(lieutikh/ (with or without te/xnh)
the art of fishing, Plat.

a glade or
grove, Lat. saltus, Hom.;
grove, Od., Hdt., etc.

from grief,
to be ill at ease, be distraught, Il.:
to be beside oneself, Hom., Soph.

on or
at both sides, Il.;
with both hands at once, id=Il.

Pass.
to be undone, kata\ ti/ deu=r' a)nefqa/rhs;
by what ill luck came you hither? Ar.

a rival in love, tino/s
for another, Ar.:
a rival, Plat.

Mid.,
to exchange one thing
for another:

comp. a)nwte/rw, absol.
higher, Aesch.;
further, Hdt.

adv. of place
from above, from on high, Hdt., Trag., etc.; u(/datos a)/nwqen genome/nou, i. e. rain, Thuc.:
from the upper country, from inland, id=Thuc.

Apeiraean, Od.;
Apeire =
limitless-land, an imaginary place.

to give up in despair, to despair, NTest.; (others
to hope to receive from another);
to drive to despair, tina/ Anth.

to guide aright, to direct, govern, id=Soph.;
to correct, chastise, Eur.: c. inf.
to direct one to do a thing, Aesch.

Adv. of a)/pneustos, a)p. e)/xein
to hold one's breath, Plat.;
without drawing breath, Dem.

devoted to enjoyment, Arist.;
producing enjoyment, id=Arist.:adv., a)polaustikw=s zh=n to live a life
of pleasure, id=Arist.

when it stands alone it usually expects a negative answer, like Lat. num? attic; so a)=ra mh/;
num vero? Aesch.:for an affirmative answer, a)=r' ou); a)=r' ou)xi/;
nonne vero? is used, Soph., etc.

of or
for reckoning, arithmetical, Plat.: h( a)riqmhtikh/ (sc. te/xnh)
arithmetic, id=Plat.

of oracles,
to utter, proclaim, tell of, id=Soph.;
to speak out concerning a thing, Aesch.

of or
for the flute, Plat.; h( -kh/ (sc. te/xnh)
flute-playing, id=Plat.

to lie in the court-yard, of cattle, Od.;
to pass the night, lodge, Eur.; of soldiers,
to bivouac, Hdt.

of or
for an autocrat: adv. -kw=s,
despotically, Plut.

of things,
to get rid of, di/yan Il.;
to shed its blossoms, of plants, Od.;
to slacken its force, of a dart, Il.

a mist, Lat. caligo, Od.;
a mist over the eyes of one dying, Il.; or of a person deprived of the power of knowing others, id=Il.metaph.
gloom, trouble, Aesch.

of solids,
the chaff that flies off in winnowing, in pl., Il.;
the down on fruits, Anth.

of or
for cattle-driving: h( bohlatikh/ (sc. te/xnh)
the herdsman's art, Plat.

Lat. fremitus, any loud noise, as the
crackling of fire, Il.;
roaring of a storm, Aesch.;
neighing of horses, id=Aesch.

EPEXEGETIC, where ga/r is used to begin a promised narration, lekte/a a(\ gignw/skw: e)/xei ga\r h( xw/ra pedi/a ka/llista I must relate what I know;
now, the country has most beautiful plains, Xen.; so, after the introductory forms, ske/yasqe de/, dh=lon de/, tekmh/rion de/, martu/rion de/, me/giston de/, Plat., etc.; tou/tou de\ tekmh/rion: to/de ga/r . . , Hdt.:in a)lla\ ga/r, a clause must be supplied between a)lla/ and ga/r, as, a)lla\ ga\r h)/kousa
but [say no more], for I heard, Aesch.

a question, like Lat. nam, Engl.
why, what, ti/s ga/r se h(=ken;
why who hath sent thee? Il.; ti/ ga/r;
quid enim? i. e. it must be so, Soph.

a milk-pail, Od.:
a water-bucket, Hdt.;
any round vessel, a bee-hive, Anth.;
a drinking-bowl, Theocr.

metaph.
to taste, feel, douro\s a)kwkh=s, o)i+stou= geu/sasqai Hom.; geuso/meq' a)llh/lwn e)gxei/ais
let us try one another with the spear, Il.:
to taste the sweets of, a)rxh=s, e)leuqeri/hs Hdt.;
to have experience of, mo/xqwn, pe/nqous Soph., Eur.

of or
for geometry, geometrical, Plat.: gewmetrikh\ (sc. te/xnh),
geometry, id=Plat.

mostly in pl. *gi/gantes,
the Giants, a savage race destroyed by the gods, Od.;
the sons of Gaia, Hes.

of or
for cookery: adv. -kw=s,
like a cook, artistically, Ar.

Dep.: of persons,
to hurt, do a mischief to, Hom.; mh/ me dhlh/setai (epic for -htai) Od.; so in Hdt.;
to hurt by magic potions, Theocr.

as interrog., ti/ dh/ pote;
what in the world? quid tandem? id=Dem.; po/soi dh/ pote; how many
do you suppose? id=Dem.

perhaps, it may be, Il.; in attic
doubtless, I suppose, I presume, of course, Lat. scilicet, ou) dh/pou tlhto/n Aesch., etc.: often in phrases, i)/ste ga\r dh/ pou, me/mnhsqe ga\r dh/ pou Dem.; so, as interrog. implying an affirm. answer, th\n ai)xma/lwton ka/toisqa dh/ pou;
I presume you know, Soph.

a runaway, Lat. fugitivus, basile/os
from the king, Hdt.:
a runaway slave, id=Hdt.

hard to use, nearly useless, Xen.;
intractable, id=Xen.:adv. -tws e)/xein
to be in distress, Plut.

strengthd. for ei),
if really, if indeed, Hom., etc.; also,
even if, even though, id=Hom.

if anywhere, if at all, Lat. si-cubi, Hom., etc.; ei)/ ti/ pou e)sti/n,
if it is
any way possible, Od.

of or
for peace, peaceful, Plat., etc.: adv. -kw=s,
peaceably, Xen.

to land one
from a ship,
disembark, id=Thuc.

OF TIME, e)c ou(= or e)c ou(=te [xro/nou], Lat. ex quo, since, Hom., attic; e)k tou= or e)k toi=o
from that time, Il.; e)k pollou= (sc. xro/nou)
for a long time, Thuc.

to draw, drag, Lat. traho, with a notion of force, podo\s e(/lke
began to drag [the dead body] by the foot, Il.;
to draw ships down to the sea, Od.; of mules,
to draw a chariot, id=Od.;
to draw the plough
through the field, id=Od.

to\ *(ellhniko/n
the Greeks collectively, Hdt.;
the Greek soldiery, Xen.

c. acc.
to appease, Hom.;
to make up for, Xen.

entry.etym:
from ei)/kw, of which we have 3rd sg. imperf. ei)=ke,
it seemed good, Il.; fut. ei)/cw,
will be like, Ar.

entry.sense:
to pour wine
over a thing, Il.;
to pour a libation, Od.

e)pi\ ple/on
still more, Hdt.;
before, Lat. coram, h)=gon au)to\n e)pi\ ta\ koina/ id=Hdt.

of Place, denoting Rest
upon, as in e)pi/keimai, or Motion,
upon or
over, as in e)pibai/nw;
to or
towards, as in e)pari/steros, e)pide/cios;
against, as in e)pai/+ssw, e)pistrateu/w;
up to a point, as in e)pitele/w;
over or
beyond boundaries, as in e)pine/momai, e)pergasi/a.

Pass.
to grow up after, as posterity, Lat. succrescere, id=Hdt.;
to grow up as a successor, id=Hdt.

of men,
conspicuous, famous, distinguished by rank, Hdt.;
notable, for well or ill, Thuc., Xen.

of or
for a statuary: h( -kh (sc. te/xnh),
the art of statuary, Luc.

the furthest part, edge, border, verge, Hom., Hdt., attic: in pl.
the borders, Hdt.;
the extremities of the world, id=Hdt.

on, for or
during the day, the day through, Od.;
by day, Pind.

to oversee, observe, survey, of the sun, Hom.:then of the gods,
to watch over, observe, take notice of, Od., Hdt., etc.; of a general going his rounds, Thuc.;
to visit the sick, Xen.

of or
for driving, Plat.: h( -kh/ (sc. te/xnh)
the art of driving, id=Plat.

from morn, i. e.
at dawn, at break of day, Hom., etc.;
this morning, Od.

of or
for a surgeon: h( -kh/ (sc. te/xnh),
surgery, medicine, Hdt., Plat., etc.

peculiar, separate, distinct, e)/qnos i)/dion Hdt.; i)/dioi/ tines qeoi/ Ar.; i)/dion h)\ a)/lloi
peculiar and different from others, Plat.;
strange, unaccustomed, i)di/oisin u(menai/oisi Eur.

any loud sound: the shout or
cry of men, Il.;
the sound of the lyre, Od.; of the wind, of a fire, Il.

for kaq' a(/,
according as, just as, Xen.: so kaqa/per, ionic kata/per, Hdt., Ar., etc.:strengthd., kaqa/per ei), ionic kata/per ei),
like as if, exactly as, Hdt., Plat.; kaqa/per a)/n Dem.; kaqa/per a)\n ei) Plat., etc.

of or
for beautiful dances, Eur., Ar.: o( k. a spring near Eleusis,
the fount of goodly dances, Hhymn., Eur.

a dry stalk, Lat. palea, stipula, a chip of wood, Ar.: in pl.
the dry sticks of cinnamon, Hdt.;
dry twigs, chips, straws, bits of wool, such as birds make nests of, Ar.

preparation, e)n kataskeuh=| tou= pole/mou
in preparing for it, Thuc.;
the equipment of ships, engines, etc., id=Thuc.

a sudden turn or
end, a close, conclusion, Aesch.; of death, Soph., Thuc.: in drama,
the catastrophe, Luc.

to lie sick or
wounded, lie in misery, Hom., Soph., etc.;
to lie at the mercy of the conqueror, Aesch.

any sharp sound, such as
the twang of a bow, Il.;
the scream of cranes, Hom.;
the grunting of swine, Od.;
the hissing of serpents, Aesch.;
the barking of dogs, Xen.:also of song, Soph.; kl. du/sfatos, of Cassandra-prophecies, Aesch.

of or
for embellishment: h( -kh/ (sc. te/xnh),
the art of embellishment, Plat.

more dog-like, i. e.
more shameless, more audacious, Hom.;
more horrible, ku/nteron a)/llo pot' e)/tlhs Od.

to receive as produce or
profit, Ar., Plat.;
to purchase Ar.

to rub smooth, pound in a mortar, Lat. levigare, Hdt.;
to grind with the teeth, Xen.: generally,
to crush, extirpate, Hdt.

a scale, husk, l. w)|ou= an egg-
shell, Ar.;
the cup of a filbert, Anth.

adv.
shrilly, Hom.;
clearly, Il.:neut. as adv., ligu\ me/lpesqai Hes., Aesch.

to abuse, revile, Hdt., attic;
to rebuke, Xen.:Mid.
to rail at one another, Ar.

to visit, ne/on meqe/peis;
dost thou come but now
to visit us? Od.

of or
for measuring, Plat.: h( -kh/ (sc. te/xnh)
mensuration, id=Plat.

of or
for metre, metrical, Arist.: ta\ -ka/ and h( -kh/ (sc. te/xnh),
prosody, id=Arist.

after interrogatives, it mostly takes somewhat of an objective force, ti/ mh/n;
quid vero? what
then? i. e.
of course, naturally so, Aesch., etc.; ti/ mh\n ou);
well, why not? Eur.; pw=s mh/n;
well, but how . . ? Xen.

with Ind., implying a negat. answer,
surely not, you don't mean to say that, Lat. num? whereas with ou) an affirm. answer is expected, Lat. nonne? a)=r' ou) te/qnhke;
surely he is dead, is he not? a)=ra mh\ te/qnhke;
surely he is not dead, is he?:when ou) and mh/ appear in consecutive clauses, each negat. retains its proper force, ou) si=g' a)ne/cei mhde\ deili/an a)rei=s;
will you not be silent, and
will you be cowardly? i. e. be silent and be not cowardly, Soph.

of or
for letting out: h( misqwtikh/, = misqarnikh/,
a mercenary trade, Plat.

= mnhmei=on
a monument, Plat.;
an epitaph, Arist.

the belly, paunch, Il., Hdt.;
the womb, Il.: metaph., of
earth, gremium telluris, Eur.

of or
for a ship, do/ru nh/ion or nh/ion alone,
ship-timber, Hom.

metaph.
like a child, childish, silly, Hom., Hes.;
without forethought, Hom., Aesch.

of or
for a herdsman's life, nomadic, pastoral, Arist.:adv. -kw=s,
like Nomads, Strab.

a way, path, track, road, highway: potamou= o(do/s
the course of a river, Xen.;
the path of the heavenly bodies, Eur.

of or
from the whole world (h( oi)koume/nh); of Eccl. Councils,
oecumenical.

of or
