to go, come, Od.;
to walk, i. e.
to live, Soph.

of or
for an omen: h( -kh/ (sc.te/xnh),
augury, Plat.

o(/pws is used as the echo to a preceding pw=s; in dialogue:
A. kai\ pw=s;
B. o(/pws; [d'ye ask]
how? Ar.;
A. pw=s me xrh\ kalei=n;
B. o(/pws; id=Ar.

of or
for the desires, appetitive, Arist.; to\ o)rektiko/n,
the appetites, id=Arist.

to set in motion, qumo\n o(rm.
to gasp out one's life, Aesch.;
to excite, urge, Pind.

of or
for bird-catching: h( -kh/ (sc. te/xnh),
