anything made of such trees,
a goad, Hes.;
a lance, Eur.

still more generally,
a sound, of the harp, Hhymn.;
the din of battle, Hes.

for o(/t' a)/n (o(/te a)/n), adverb of Time,
whenever, Lat. quandocunque, foll. by Subjunct., Hom., etc.; in epic also o(/te ken Il.: ei)s o(/te ken
until such time as. . , Od.: o(/tan ta/xista, Lat. quum primum, Xen.

= o(/ ti,
wherefore, o(tih\ ti/;
why so? wherefore so? id=Ar.

any loud noise, as
the din of battle, Hes.;
the rattling of chariots, Aesch.;
the crash of thunder, Soph.; also of the flute, gluku\n au)lw=n o)/t. id=Soph.

elliptic, in interrogative replies, where
yes must be supplied, tou/tous a)gaqou\s e)no/misas; Answ. ou) ga/r . . ;
yes, for why shouldn't I? yes; why not? Ar.

